          "path": "_m/g/f/h/t/glenmoriston-wp/roderick-mackenzie-grave-geogr.jpg",
          "filename": "Roderick Mackenzie' grave. - geograph.org.uk - 942698.jpg",
          "caption": "Roderick Mackenzie' grave. The grave is hidden on the N side of the road a short distance from the better known memorial cairn where he was captured, which is some 200 yds away to the S.\nMackenzie was an officer in the Jacobite army who bore a marked resemblance to Bonnie Prince Charlie. When pursued and caught he allowed his captors to believe they had captured the prince. This took the heat of the pursuit of Prince Charles for a time. Mackenzie was beheaded &amp; his head sent to Fort Augustus for identification but by then was unrecognizable.",
          "alt": "Roderick Mackenzie' grave. The grave is hidden on the N side of the road a short distance from the better known memorial cairn where he was captured, which is some 200 yds away to the S.\nMackenzie was an officer in the Jacobite army who bore a marked resemblance to Bonnie Prince Charlie. When pursued and caught he allowed his captors to believe they had captured the prince. This took the heat of the pursuit of Prince Charles for a time. Mackenzie was beheaded &amp; his head sent to Fort Augustus for identification but by then was unrecognizable.",
          "width": 640,
          "height": 426,
          "mimeType": "image/jpeg",
          "license": "CC BY-SA 2.0",
          "artist": "ronnie leask",
